# The kernel's burn-down list against termlens: one `fixture/aspect` per line (tests/oracle.rs).
# Lower is better, and it only shrinks — a key that stops disagreeing must be removed.
# Seeded 2026-09-19 at 21.
#   21 → 7  slice 3a: surfaced what vt100 0.15 tracks (grid rows — the wrap/text defect — cursor
#           position and visibility, italic/underline/reverse, title, alternate screen, input modes).
#    7 → 3  slice 3b: vt100 0.16 and its callbacks — cursor shape (DECSCUSR), the query responder
#           (DA1 here; DA2, DSR, CPR and text-area size agreed on first contact), dim.
#    3 → 0  slice 3c: blink, conceal and strikethrough through the attribute shadow ported from
#           termlens (src/shadow.rs); colon-form colours agreed on first contact.
#
# EMPTY: over this corpus the kernel and termlens agree. A new fixture that disagrees lands its
# keys here deliberately — the list is the burn-down, and it starts again from what it measures.
